AXES:        C1b I1 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with struct-based config and a flag-gated
  sanitization check. Both --enable-exec and --enable-diag must be supplied for
  the /exec endpoint to execute commands. A --strict-mode flag enables injection
  character checking, but omitting --strict-mode bypasses sanitization entirely.
  The cmd query parameter flows directly into system().

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — two flags + struct):
  mechanism:  Two CLI flags (--enable-exec, --enable-diag) stored in
              struct server_config fields (enable_exec, enable_diag)
  check:      double boolean guard in callback_exec():
              `if (!cfg->enable_exec || !cfg->enable_diag)`
  complexity: two conditions, one struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads cmd from request->map_url
              cmd pointer passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — no snprintf, no copy, no urldecode step

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated check):
  mechanism:  --strict-mode CLI flag stored in cfg->strict_mode
              enables has_injection() check in callback_exec()
  bypass:     omit --strict-mode — check is never called
  check:      `if (cfg->strict_mode && has_injection(cmd))` → return 400
              blocks: |  ;  &  `  $  (  )  <  >  {  }  \n

SINK:        system() in callback_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — additions after callback_default():
    1. server_config struct: two exec gates + strict_mode field (C2+S3)
    2. has_injection():      checks for 12 shell metacharacters (S3)
    3. callback_exec():      C2 two-flag gate + S3 check + I1 direct system()
    4. main():               three flag parsing into cfg struct + endpoint reg.

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18103 --enable-exec --enable-diag
           (omit --strict-mode to bypass S3 sanitization)
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18103/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_103_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_103_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass (C2): supplying only one of the two flags (or neither) → 403.
  sani bypass (S3): omitting --strict-mode disables has_injection() entirely;
                    all metacharacters including > ; | pass to system().

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - With --strict-mode active, the payload id>/tmp/marker is blocked (400)
    because '>' is in the injection character set.
